  "notes": [
    [
      "The four films count once each.",
      "Comedy Central re-cut the 2007–09 films into sixteen half-hour episodes and aired them as season 5. It is the same footage either way, so listing both would count the same watch twice. The films are the form the work was written and released in, and the source article gives the sixteen parts no titles of their own — so this list carries four film rows, each naming its runtime and the season 5 episodes it was broadcast as. That is 169 rows; the sixteen-part reading would be 181."
    ],
    [
      "Production order, not the order Fox aired it.",
      "Fox broadcast the first 72 episodes out of the order they were made, so no box set, streaming season or episode list matches a strict airdate sort. This follows the production seasons, like the source article does, with the four eras in the order they reached an audience."
    ],
    [
      "Nothing is weighted.",
      "Wikipedia documents one running time for the series and none per episode, so there is no verifiable per-row number to weight with; every row counts one. The four film rows are feature length and their notes say so rather than carrying a weight the rest of the list could not match."
    ],
    [
      "The specials are still to come.",
      "Hulu has ordered three extended-length specials, the first due in 2027. That one is listed already, marked not out yet; the other two join once they are dated."
    ],
    "Titles and airdates machine-read from Wikipedia's List of Futurama episodes, the season articles and the four film articles, and the special's due date from the Futurama article; every season's count is asserted against the list article's own series overview, and the overall episode numbering asserted contiguous, before this builds."
  ],
